    "title": "Mavericks' Anthony Davis sends out cryptic 'they never see that part' message - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Paolo Mariano ,\n2 hours ago\nJerome Miron-Imagn Images The post appeared first on .\nAfter yet another injury-riddled campaign, fans are fervently hoping that Anthony Davis can stay healthy to lead the Dallas Mavericks back to the NBA Finals.\nDavis only played nine games for the Mavericks last season following the league-altering midseason trade with the Los Angeles Lakers. In his debut for Dallas, he strained his left adductor, which sidelined him for 18 games.\nWith Kyrie Irving out for an extended period with a torn ACL, Davis will have to carry the cudgels for the Mavericks . Aside from the physical toll, the 10-time All-Star will have to remain mentally tough to embrace the role of leader.\nHowever, it looks like Davis is already dealing with some emotional stress ahead of training camp. He posted an Instagram Story, which many would view as cryptic .\n“I broke bread at times when I could’ve just fed myself. They never see that part,” read the message.\nIt’s hard to speculate what the 32-year-old Davis is talking about. Is it personal? Or does it have something to do with the Mavericks? Or even the Lakers? Davis has always been the silent type. He rarely shares about his life, unlike other stars.\nIt is not the first time that Davis posted something cryptic since he was traded to the Mavericks. In August, fans grew concerned after he posted an Instagram Story of a sad emoji and a prayer emoji over a black background.\nWhatever he is going through these days, he still has a job to do. Dallas will open training camp a few days from now, and Davis is expected to show up. He underwent a procedure to repair a detached retina in July.\nLast season, he averaged 24.7 points on 51.6% shooting, 11.6 rebounds, 3.5 assists, 1.2 steals, and 2.2 blocks.\nHe will lead the charge for the Mavericks, along with PJ Washington, Klay Thompson, D’Angelo Russell, and Cooper Flagg.",
